---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import FaqList from '../components/FaqList.astro';
import { GENERAL_FAQ, IMAGE_FAQ } from '../content/faq';
---
<SiteLayout title="FAQ | ConvertAnyFile" description="Answers about private browser conversion, batch limits, image formats, quality settings, retries, local processing, and how ConvertAnyFile handles files.">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="site-container hero-inner"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>FAQ</span></div><span class="eyebrow">Help</span><h1>Questions about ConvertAnyFile.</h1><p>How browser-first conversion works, why the product has safety limits, what the current image engine can do, and what users should expect from conversion quality and privacy.</p></div></section>

<section class="content-wide-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="content-intro-grid"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">Before you convert</span><h2>The important answers in one place.</h2><p>ConvertAnyFile is designed around a simple rule: explain what the browser can do, do not pretend unsupported workflows are available, and keep the conversion path understandable when something goes wrong.</p></div><div class="content-summary-card"><strong>Current live category</strong><p>Image conversion is live now. Other categories shown on the platform are planned until their own browser-first engines are implemented and tested.</p></div></div><ul class="content-checklist"><li>Local converters process supported file bytes in the browser session.</li><li>The current image workflow supports batch conversion, cancel, retry, individual downloads, and ZIP results.</li><li>File signatures and runtime codec capabilities are checked instead of trusting extensions alone.</li><li>Safety limits protect browser memory and CPU rather than protecting a conversion server.</li></ul></div></section>

<section class="content-wide-section white"><div class="site-container"><FaqList items={GENERAL_FAQ} title="Platform questions" intro="Accounts, local processing, batches, cancellation, failures, and how the platform is designed to grow." /></div></section>
<section class="content-wide-section"><div class="site-container"><FaqList items={IMAGE_FAQ} title="Image converter questions" intro="Image formats, quality settings, transparency, RAW files, memory use, and what conversion can or cannot improve." /></div></section>

<section class="content-wide-section white"><div class="site-container"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">Need more context?</span><h2>Use the format guides before converting blindly.</h2><p>The guides explain why different formats exist and what trade-offs to expect before you choose an output.</p></div><div class="related-grid"><a class="related-card" href="/guides/jpg-vs-png/">JPG vs PNG <span>→</span></a><a class="related-card" href="/guides/webp-vs-avif/">WebP vs AVIF <span>→</span></a><a class="related-card" href="/guides/heic-explained/">HEIC explained <span>→</span></a><a class="related-card" href="/guides/image-quality-compression/">Image quality & compression <span>→</span></a></div></div></section>
</SiteLayout>
